EXAM AND OBJECTIVE SCORING
Study v2.1: 60 tasks, comprising 20 mathematical/logical reasoning, 20 data reasoning, 10 instruction-following and 10 coding tasks. It is NOT a 30-math/30-code suite.
Public prompts: datasets/study_v2/public/tasks.json; keys and coding tests: datasets/study_v2/private/answer_keys.json. Plain-text reviewer copies are in exam/.
The 50 non-coding keys were independently recomputed from the prompts. The ten references passed all 4076 hidden coding cases, both locally and in the actual Docker sandbox. Reviewer also rejected 26 plausible wrong programs.
Non-coding primary success requires exact required JSON schema/types, correct answer and valid FINAL_JSON presentation. Numeric-equivalent float/string answers may receive secondary substantive credit while failing schema. Duplicate keys, invalid/non-finite JSON, non-stop finish reasons, truncation and missing final answers have distinct failure handling.
Coding: FINAL_CODE fenced Python function; deterministic hidden-case execution, no input mutation, plus specified output-alias constraints. Equivalent valid solutions accepted. Imports, dangerous operations and private attributes forbidden; literal module constants and postponed annotations permitted. Allowed builtins are disclosed in the coding prompts.
Model code NEVER executes on the host. Docker is used by the evaluator, not by the model. Pinned image: python@sha256:a6e34c598f2467ed0e9a8d349809fcd8b5c603269512df273a0bb1784edc11b1
Sandbox: network disabled, read-only root, unprivileged uid/gid 65534, capabilities dropped, no-new-privileges, 256MiB RAM/swap, 1 CPU, 32 processes, 10s CPU limit, 20s host wall timeout, limited tmpfs, forced container cleanup. Infrastructure errors are unscored, not counted as model failures. CPU limit/nonzero execution are separate model-code failures.
Docker preflight, ordinary failure probes, recursion/builtin/constant/annotation checks, 20-second wall-timeout and cleanup checks passed. Proof files are in environment/.
Primary deterministic scores stay fixed. Review ALL final answers separately for interpretation, preserving disagreements and reasons; generated reasoning is archived, not assumed to reveal every internal computation. Do not silently revise keys after observing quantization results.

PRIOR FAILURES / FIXES (DIAGNOSTIC ONLY)
1. Original small custom pilot produced low arithmetic/extraction scores. It was insufficient to conclude general model inability; preserve raw pilot and component outcomes.
2. Published GSM8K, 20-question diagnostic: direct short prompt 5/20 strict correct; post-hoc numeric fallback 8/20; 13 formatting failures. Asking for worked solutions produced 20/20 on the same small sample. Prompt sensitivity and format requirements mattered; this is not a contamination-free accuracy claim.
3. Reasoning enabled with 4096 context/2048 output: stopped after seven completed questions; three correct and four truncated; no completed wrong numeric answers. Not a full 20-question score.
4. Four selected truncation retries at 8192 context/6144 output: three correct, one truncated; about 602s total and 16360 output tokens. Selected retries are not representative accuracy estimates.
5. Unrestricted-reasoning independent calibration repeated reasoning after solving an elementary item. Interrupted, excluded from kept scores. Bounded calibration (2048 reasoning budget, 32768 context/12288 output) passed all four fresh questions; total generation ~309s, no truncation or infrastructure errors. This small pilot checks the pipeline, not difficulty/coverage of the full exam. It preceded moving embeddings to CUDA; a separate all-GPU smoke check passed afterward. Calibration timing is excluded from comparisons.
6. v1 answer/task and hidden-test defects were revised in v2. v2 sandbox omitted ord/chr/divmod/frozenset/pow and rejected constants/annotations; these were fixed and verified. Bundle-path bug fixed. DAT-06 interval gap added. History and audit records preserve the prior versions; never benchmark using these obsolete keys.
7. '34/34 layers offloaded' alone left 1030.62 MiB input embeddings host-mapped. Explicit tensor override moved them to CUDA before kept Q8 measurements. Startup evidence is included.

